## Findings this work item is fixing (all reproduced live, not inferred)

- P0-A: the worker advanced an entire run inside ONE transaction (run.py owned
  the session and committed once after `run_once`). Live evidence: a run that
  had already spent 5 minutes and six DeepSeek calls still read
  `queued / progress 0 / started_at NULL` from the API, with a matching
  `idle in transaction 00:05:07` backend. Consequence: no status, progress,
  heartbeat or SSE event is visible while the analysis runs; a crash rolls the
  whole run back; `recover_stale_runs` can never see the heartbeat.
- P0-B: `FIXTURE_MODE=true` cannot run an analysis at all.
  `FixtureModelProvider.responses` is empty by default and the worker passes no
  `fixture_key`, so every stage resolved to `{}` -> `EmptyModelContentError` ->
  the run was parked `needs_attention` within ~3s. This contradicts the
  key-free promise in compose.prototype.yaml and section 8.
- P1: `needs_attention` is not in the backend terminal set, so the SSE stream
  of a parked run never closes (browser EventSource hangs; 50ms DB poll loop).
- P0-C (found while testing the fixture path): the READY report hook wrote the
  evidence funnel's warning STRINGS into `EvidenceReview.reconciliationFindings`,
  which is typed `list[dict]`. Validation failed inside a try/except that only
  logged, so any run whose evidence set carried a warning (majority low-trust
  sources, or zero opposing facts) reached `ready` with NO report at all. The
  earlier live run happened to have real Exa sources and no warning, which is
  why this never surfaced.
- P1-D: `AnalysisRun.origin_modes` was never written. Every run reported
  `originModes: []`, so nothing could distinguish a live analysis from a fixture
  one - AGENTS.md section 8 forbids hiding the fixture/cached/live marker.
- P1-E (NOT fixed here, reported): `packages/contracts/openapi.json` holds 56
  operations while the app now serves 69. Eleven paths (invites, invites/redeem,
  invites revoke, calibration, mentor-reviews, question-clarifier, sandbox,
  sandbox/preview, export, portfolio, purge) never had contracts regenerated,
  so the web app cannot type them from the generated package. This predates
  this branch and belongs to the contract/integration lane (CCR + regeneration).

## Scope

- Stage boundaries become commit boundaries (claim, stage entry, packets,
  each lens, enrichment, stage completion, terminal transition, report).
- Precise parking: park the run the worker actually claimed instead of
  re-claiming the queue head.
- Deterministic fixture stage responses so the key-free path reaches `ready`.
- SSE closes on `needs_attention` as well.
- Structured funnel quality findings so a warning degrades the report's stated
  confidence instead of deleting the report.
- `originModes` recorded on the run (idempotent, additive).

